From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:05:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: Vote MX from the display
 clock controller

The display clock controller voted MMCX only. Its PLLs run on MX
(vendor tree: dispcc vdd_mm + vdd_mx), and nothing else on the display
path votes MX once the MDSS driver has taken over from the boot splash.
MX then follows only the other voters: on the OnePlus Pad 4 the USB
controller's CX vote (required-opps nom, which the RPMh dependency rule
carries to MX) held it while the controller was active. When the
controller runtime-suspends, MX follows the ADSP's changing votes (sensor
hub streaming), and the panel shows torn / ghost frames while the MDP PLL
runs at up to 1.95 GHz.

Give dispcc its MX vote: power-domains MMCX + MX, required-opps
low_svs + nom. qcom_cc_really_probe() attaches both domains and sets
each required-opps, and the display GDSCs keep the controller runtime
active while they are on, so the vote is held exactly while the display
is powered and dropped when it is off. NOM covers the MDP PLL at 650 MHz
MDP (taycan_eko_t at 1.95 GHz).

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index 68a0f953efb7..f39f3dac2a08 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -4967,8 +4967,10 @@
 				 <&mdss_dsi1_phy DSI_BYTE_PLL_CLK>,
 				 <&mdss_dsi1_phy DSI_PIXEL_PLL_CLK>;
 
-			power-domains = <&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MMCX>;
-			required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
+			power-domains = <&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MMCX>,
+					<&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MX>;
+			required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>,
+					<&rpmhpd_opp_nom>;
 
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 			#power-domain-cells = <1>;
